<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samudera Pasai Sultanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 13th century–1524</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Samudra Pasai, Pasai Sultanate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Samudera Pasai Sultanate was a Muslim port kingdom on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhokseumawe">Lhokseumawe</a>, from the late 13th century. Its first known sultan, Malik al-Salih, died in 1297, making it one of the earliest Islamic states in maritime South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-battuta">Ibn Battuta</a> visited it in the 1340s. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> and gold port, it was occupied by the Portuguese in 1521 and absorbed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> in 1524.</p></div>
